        "original_id": "a0981aa3-dbfb-539c-8aa9-0abbe8c1c978",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Masa Takayama\n- Restaurants: Tetsu, Masa, Bar Masa\n- Places: Tribeca, Manhattan, New York City, Kuroiso, Tochigi, Paradise, Nevada, Las Vegas Strip, Aria Resort & Casino\n- Concepts: modern Japanese cuisine, yakitori, grilled fare, Michelin stars\n\nFacts:\n- Masa Takayama was born on 1 May 1954 in Kuroiso, Tochigi, Japan.\n- Masa Takayama is the chef and owner of Masa, a three-Michelin-starred Japanese and sushi restaurant in Manhattan, New York City.\n- Masa Takayama also owns Bar Masa, which has one location adjacent to Masa in New York City and another in the Aria Resort & Casino on the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\n- Tetsu is a modern Japanese restaurant in the Tribeca neighborhood of New York City.\n- Masa Takayama conceived Tetsu.\n- Tetsu serves a yakitori-based menu with an emphasis on grilled fare.",
